From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 12:05:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 35/66] mac80211: ath11k: give a 6 GHz capable radio's 5 GHz
 band HT and VHT

ath11k patch 108 (for upstream): a QCN9074-family radio covering 5 and
6 GHz had its 5 GHz band registered with HE but without HT and VHT
capabilities, so on 5 GHz it used legacy rates only: the C-360's
QCN9072 associated to an 802.11ax AP at 24-54 Mbit/s as a client.
Set the 5 GHz band's HT and VHT whenever it was registered with
channels.

Bump PKG_RELEASE.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
---
 package/kernel/mac80211/Makefile              |  2 +-
 ...apable-radio-s-5-GHz-band-HT-and-VHT.patch | 39 +++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 40 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 package/kernel/mac80211/patches/ath11k/108-wifi-ath11k-give-a-6-GHz-capable-radio-s-5-GHz-band-HT-and-VHT.patch

diff --git a/package/kernel/mac80211/Makefile b/package/kernel/mac80211/Makefile
index 5f323c3ba1..4226722a83 100644
--- a/package/kernel/mac80211/Makefile
+++ b/package/kernel/mac80211/Makefile
@@ -12,7 +12,7 @@ PKG_NAME:=mac80211
 
 PKG_SOURCE_VERSION:=7.2
 PKG_VERSION:=$(subst -,_,$(PKG_SOURCE_VERSION))
-PKG_RELEASE:=18
+PKG_RELEASE:=19
 PKG_LICENSE:=GPL-2.0-only
 PKG_LICENSE_FILES:=COPYING
 
diff --git a/package/kernel/mac80211/patches/ath11k/108-wifi-ath11k-give-a-6-GHz-capable-radio-s-5-GHz-band-HT-and-VHT.patch b/package/kernel/mac80211/patches/ath11k/108-wifi-ath11k-give-a-6-GHz-capable-radio-s-5-GHz-band-HT-and-VHT.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..21a8361e3e
--- /dev/null
+++ b/package/kernel/mac80211/patches/ath11k/108-wifi-ath11k-give-a-6-GHz-capable-radio-s-5-GHz-band-HT-and-VHT.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,39 @@
+From: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
+Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 12:00:00 -0500
+Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: give a 6 GHz capable radio's 5 GHz band HT and
+ VHT
+
+ath11k_mac_setup_ht_vht_cap() sets the 5 GHz band's HT and VHT
+capabilities only for a single_pdev_only device or a radio that does
+not support 6 GHz. A QCN9074 can cover 5 GHz as well as 6 GHz, and
+ath11k_mac_setup_channels_rates() then registers its 5 GHz band too, with
+its HE capabilities (ath11k_mac_setup_he_cap() sets HE for any 5 GHz
+capable radio), but without HT and VHT. mac80211 can't use HE on 5 GHz
+without them, so on that band such a radio uses legacy rates only: on
+an Arista C-360, its QCN9072 radio associated to an 802.11ax AP on 5 GHz
+at 24-54 Mbit/s (no MCS), where `iw phy` showed its 5 GHz band with HE
+capabilities and no HT or VHT ones.
+
+Give the 5 GHz band HT and VHT whenever it was registered with channels,
+which ath11k_mac_setup_channels_rates() does before this runs.
+
+Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
+Signed-off-by: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
+---
+--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/mac.c
++++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/mac.c
+@@ -5765,9 +5765,12 @@
+ 						    rate_cap_rx_chainmask);
+ 	}
+ 
++	/* A 6 GHz capable radio may cover 5 GHz as well, as a QCN9074 does:
++	 * its 5 GHz band, where one was registered, needs HT and VHT as much
++	 * as any other radio's.
++	 */
+ 	if (cap->supported_bands & WMI_HOST_WLAN_5G_CAP &&
+-	    (ar->ab->hw_params.single_pdev_only ||
+-	     !ar->supports_6ghz)) {
++	    ar->mac.sbands[NL80211_BAND_5GHZ].n_channels) {
+ 		band = &ar->mac.sbands[NL80211_BAND_5GHZ];
+ 		ht_cap = cap->band[NL80211_BAND_5GHZ].ht_cap_info;
+ 		if (ht_cap_info)
